type: software
title: "Two-qutrit entanglement invisible to real witnesses under every local filter"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Both parts of Conjecture 9 of Shen, Chen and Bian (real entanglement witnesses after local unitaries, or after invertible local filters, detect every entangled state) are false: an explicit full-rank two-qutrit state with positive-definite partial transpose is detected by a complex witness, while every filtered real witness and every limit of such witnesses has expectation above 8.5e-10 on it, also on a ball of radius 8e-10. Part (i) fails for a qubit and a ququart, the smallest possible dimension. In every dimension the conjecture holds exactly when every exposed point of the normalised block-positive set is a limit of filtered real ones, and failures are robust. A degree-nine invariant classifies an exposed Ha-Kye family; one local ancilla qubit restores detection."
